    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Around 600 BCE, small tribal kingdoms grew into sixteen large states called Mahajanapadas, such as Magadha, Kosala, Kashi and Vajji.\nSome had kings and some were run by assemblies of leaders. Magadha grew powerful because of iron, fertile land and the Ganga.\nCities grew with trade, coins, crafts and markets."
    }
